  "notes": [
    "Content is an English working list titled Terminology, with page references rather than statements or proofs. It includes primitive/primary/secondary/ternary structure, standard type, stacks, Coherator, Hot-equivalence, test notions, modelizers, simplices/cubes, aspheric and weak-equivalence terminology, and local variants.",
    "All words and every entry were read against both C and H from the supplied halves. Whole image and each half were viewed once only. Ten specifically unresolved loci were then cropped once each by scripts/crop.py and viewed once each. No OCR, text extraction, web lookup, other page or other reader output was used.",
    "All twelve inline C doubt loci are separately adjudicated; the unmatched-parenthesis concern from C_context is also separately recorded. Removal of a doubt wrapper without changing its first textual candidate is recorded in c_doubts, and is not independently counted as a textual difference from C.",
    "The marks after 29 and within the cancelled number above functor are read as crossed 7 and underlined 41 respectively. A full stop after test in Strict test. category is preserved. The accent in local test catégory is preserved.",
    "Weak equivalence has a question mark in the reference column. Its left parenthesis has no closing mate in the visible ink; no close was supplied. The wave after Y is retained as tentative m followed by semicolon, and the X-to-Y connector remains explicitly doubtful.",
    "The two square-like drawings and all their crossing strokes are retained using the detailed C TikZ geometry, which the half confirmed. Their reference 34 is also crossed. Inventory rows separate the objects and the cancellation overlays.",
    "Inventory covers the heading, every list entry or continuation line, the three textual deletions, two inserted pieces, the branching reference diagram, each square-like drawing and cancellation, grouping curves, and the archive numeral. Underlines, commas, reference punctuation and leaders are included in their owning element rows.",
    "The map-of-objects crop was used to settle insertion placement. The top right curved stroke continues into a leader returning to the original line; it was not treated as an additional textual closing parenthesis.",
    "H emphasis is treated as an underline where applicable, so emph versus uline alone is not counted. H slash proxies between stacked groups are recorded where the manuscript has only stacked lines/grouping curves; the genuine slash after modelizer ! is retained.",
    "No mathematically substantive proof, computation, or theorem check occurred: this page is a terminology index. Reinspection of the weak-equivalence connector and missing delimiter was a transcription/parsing check, not mathematical verification."
